From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: register no render node, as mainline does

The display controller draws nothing, yet held the first render node.
Clients that take the first render node, or the display's, as their GPU
device handed it to Mesa as the device for scanout buffers, where
DRM_IOCTL_MODE_CREATE_DUMB is refused: WPE WebKit's renderer died on it.
Without the node the GPU holds renderD128 and Mesa allocates on the
primary node, as on mainline.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_drv.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_drv.c
@@ -3089,7 +3089,7 @@ static struct dma_buf *rockchip_drm_gem_prime_export(str
 DEFINE_DRM_GEM_FOPS(rockchip_drm_driver_fops);
 
 static const struct drm_driver rockchip_drm_driver = {
-	.driver_features	= DRIVER_MODESET | DRIVER_GEM | DRIVER_ATOMIC | DRIVER_RENDER,
+	.driver_features	= DRIVER_MODESET | DRIVER_GEM | DRIVER_ATOMIC,
 	.postclose		= rockchip_drm_postclose,
 	.lastclose		= rockchip_drm_lastclose,
 	.open			= rockchip_drm_open,
